      "content": "When storing poultry cooled to $41^{\\circ}\\text{F}$ or below, it must be clearly labeled with the product name, date received, and \"Use By\" date. Organize your walk-in refrigerator using a strict top-to-bottom system, keeping ready-to-eat foods at the top and raw poultry on the lowest shelves. Proper use of separate, dedicated containers minimizes any potential cross-contamination between different food types.",
